Install eksctl on Linux (Amazon Linux / Ubuntu) — Recommended for Jump Server
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
commands: curl --silent --location "https://github.com/weaveworks/eksctl/releases/latest/download/eksctl_$(uname -s)_amd64.tar.gz" -o eksctl.tar.gz
          tar -xzf eksctl.tar.gz
          sudo mv eksctl /usr/local/bin
          eksctl version
If it shows version → Installed successfully
After Installing (Very Important)
You must also install:
1️⃣ AWS CLI
command: sudo yum install awscli -y   # Amazon Linux
Configure it: 
command; aws configure
Since eksctl is working, make sure:
RUN command: aws sts get-caller-identity
If it shows your account ID → Good

to install kubectl
----------------------
commands: curl -LO "https://dl.k8s.io/release/$(curl -L -s https://dl.k8s.io/release/stable.txt)/bin/linux/amd64/kubectl"
          chmod +x kubectl
          sudo mv kubectl /usr/local/bin/
          kubectl version --client
          
